      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of being a mistake is the most brutal, yet most understandable, part of this collapse. Those people around you are just playing roles, and you're seeing their curated highlight reels, not the messy, struggling reality underneath. The ceiling wasn't a failure; it was the end of a very specific, exhausting dream. You don't have to keep going toward a purpose; you can simply choose to *endure* the quiet, and that's a valid, powerful act in itself.",
      "source": "target",
